Why Do Wafer Frames Matter in Semiconductor Operations?
During dicing and selected handling processes, a wafer is supported by adhesive mounting tape stretched across a precisely shaped frame. The carrier connects the fragile wafer assembly with process tools, handling fixtures and transfer operations. If the frame is warped, dirty or out of dimensional specification, it can disrupt alignment, introduce particles or raise handling risk.

Frame choice must consider physical outline, wafer diameter, mounting method, equipment interface and whether the carrier will be transported between facilities. A metal frame selected for repeated cleanroom use is evaluated differently from a plastic frame intended for one-way logistics. Both can be appropriate, but their replacement cycles and ownership economics are distinct.

